Phase 114 PCI resource pools and prefetch bridge windows

Build:
- Command: make -f Makefile.virt -j2
- Result: PASS; kernel linked successfully.

Default QEMU topology:
- Command: timeout 65 make -f Makefile.virt run-log QEMU_SERIAL_LOG=/tmp/avisor-phase114-final-basic.log
- virtio-net BAR4 0x4000 and BAR1 0x1000 allocated from MMIO pool; its I/O BAR0 size 0x20 received port 0.
- edu BAR0 allocated at 0x10100000; pool usage MMIO=0x105000, I/O=0x20.
- Both guest virtio-net loopback suites passed. edu liveness, factorial(10)=3628800, function reset and MSI reinitialization passed.
- QEMU terminated by timeout as expected.

Nested bridge topology:
- Command: timeout 75 qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt,virtualization=on,gic-version=3,highmem=off -cpu max -smp 2 -m 1G -device edu,bus=pcie.0,addr=0x3 -device pci-bridge,id=br1,bus=pcie.0,addr=0x4,chassis_nr=1 -device pci-bridge,id=br2,bus=br1,addr=0x1,chassis_nr=2 -device e1000,bus=br2,addr=0x2 -kernel bin_virt/kernel8.img -display none -monitor none -serial file:/tmp/avisor-phase114-final-nested.log
- Recursive enumeration reached bus 2 and allocated e1000 BAR0 MMIO 0x20000 plus BAR1 I/O 0x40.
- Both bridges configured MMIO and I/O windows; no window mismatch, allocation failure, rollback warning, PANIC or ASSERT appeared.
- QEMU terminated by timeout as expected.

Additional checks:
- pci.c compiled as part of the virt build. Standalone compile also succeeded with pre-existing macro redefinition and MSI-X signedness warnings.
- git diff --check passed for pci.c and pci.h before final documentation edits.
- Root `make -j2` is not the virt target and remains blocked by existing `boot.S` assembler errors for `UL` literal suffixes.

Coverage limits:
- The available QEMU topologies have no prefetchable BAR, so the prefetch bridge register write/readback path was not exercised by hardware emulation.
- Pool exhaustion and recursive scan failure were not injected; rollback paths were not runtime fault-injection tested.
